<!DOCTYPE html>
<html metal:use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/page"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
      xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      xmlns:metal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/metal">
<head>
  <title metal:fill-slot="title">Badge issued</title>
</head>
<body>
  <tal:t metal:fill-slot="header-title">Badge issued</tal:t>
  <tal:r metal:fill-slot="header-right">
    <a class="btn-sm btn-secondary" tal:attributes="href string:${view/portal_url}/@@pfas-lab-staff">&#8592; Lab Staff</a>
  </tal:r>
  <metal:fill fill-slot="content">
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
      This code is shown ONCE and is not kept anywhere: print the badge now. Anyone holding it can sign
      in as <strong tal:content="view/issued/name">AN1</strong> at a registered lab terminal. A lost badge
      is revoked on Lab Staff; issuing a new one revokes this one. Do not refresh or go back to this
      page: that issues another badge, and the one shown here stops working.
    </div>
    <p class="rt-line">Badge code (for a badge printer):
      <code class="badge-code" tal:content="view/issued/code_grouped">ABCD EFGH</code></p>
    <script type="application/json" id="badge-data" tal:content="structure view/issued/json">{}</script>
    <div class="rt-form">
      <button type="button" class="btn-sm btn-primary" id="badge-print">Print badge</button>
      <a class="btn-sm btn-secondary" id="badge-open" target="_blank" hidden="hidden">Open PDF</a>
    </div>
    <iframe id="badge-pdf" class="rt-preview dt-pdf" title="Badge" hidden="hidden"></iframe>
  </metal:fill>
  <tal:s metal:fill-slot="scripts">
    <script tal:attributes="src string:${view/portal_url}/++resource++senaite.pfas/vendor/pdfme/pdfme.min.js"></script>
    <script tal:attributes="src string:${view/portal_url}/++resource++senaite.pfas/badge_print.js"></script>
  </tal:s>
</body>
</html>
